[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T1. A journey through time: The secrets of Avicenna", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 151.06434631347656, 469.6398620605469, 172.77197265625]}, {"text": "7%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.70750427246094, 304.6280822753906, 207.2747344970703]}, {"text": "1.1", "bbox": [195.72799682617188, 209.6475067138672, 209.79298400878906, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.2", "bbox": [227.35400390625, 209.6475067138672, 241.4189910888672, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.3", "bbox": [258.97998046875, 209.6475067138672, 273.0449523925781, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.4", "bbox": [290.60601806640625, 209.6475067138672, 304.6709899902344, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.5", "bbox": [322.23199462890625, 209.6475067138672, 336.2969665527344, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.6", "bbox": [353.8580017089844, 209.6475067138672, 367.9229736328125, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "∑", "bbox": [387.9630126953125, 194.75196838378906, 397.0688171386719, 229.34210205078125]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [199.91200256347656, 225.5885009765625, 205.6083984375, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [231.53799438476562, 225.5885009765625, 237.23439025878906, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [263.16400146484375, 225.5885009765625, 268.8603820800781, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [294.78997802734375, 225.5885009765625, 300.4863586425781, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "7", "bbox": [326.416015625, 225.5885009765625, 332.1123962402344, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [358.0419921875, 225.5885009765625, 363.7383728027344, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "25", "bbox": [386.8190002441406, 225.5885009765625, 398.2139892578125, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "A chemist found herself in the 11 th Century, where she met the renowned physician Avicenna. In Avi-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 521.968505859375, 538.567138671875, 539.5206909179688]}, {"text": "cenna's laboratory, she discovered a blue elixir and a yellow mysterious stone. She brought them back", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 537.9085083007812, 538.5659790039062, 551.4757080078125]}, {"text": "to 2026. Determined to uncover their composition, she began her research.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 549.8644409179688, 409.9774169921875, 563.431640625]}, {"text": "Part 1. The blue elixir", "bbox": [56.29199981689453, 575.235595703125, 173.0382843017578, 590.1596069335938]}, {"text": "At first, the chemist compiled a table listing the names of the only four plants which she saw in Avicenna’s", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 594.2335205078125, 538.5841064453125, 607.8007202148438]}, {"text": "lab that could have been used to prepare the elixir, and the compounds that can be extracted from these", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 606.1885375976562, 538.5537109375, 619.7557373046875]}, {"text": "plants.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 618.1435546875, 88.17547607421875, 631.7107543945312]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Plants", "bbox": [105.25, 156.5345001220703, 133.96224975585938, 170.1017303466797]}, {"text": "Compounds that can be extracted", "bbox": [255.98899841308594, 156.5345001220703, 414.68548583984375, 170.1017303466797]}, {"text": "Zingiber", "bbox": [97.39800262451172, 187.30650329589844, 141.4370880126953, 200.8737335205078]}, {"text": "1 (C11H14O3)", "bbox": [192.0970001220703, 251.44650268554688, 254.94082641601562, 267.2128601074219]}, {"text": "2 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [317.13201904296875, 251.44650268554688, 374.3536682128906, 267.2128601074219]}, {"text": "3 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 251.44650268554688, 485.97369384765625, 267.2128601074219]}, {"text": "Hypericum", "bbox": [94.29499816894531, 277.83551025390625, 144.91282653808594, 291.4027404785156]}, {"text": "4 (C6H12O)", "bbox": [197.47299194335938, 328.82550048828125, 249.567626953125, 344.59185791015625]}, {"text": "5 (C10H12O2)", "bbox": [314.32000732421875, 328.82550048828125, 377.1639099121094, 344.59185791015625]}, {"text": "6 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 328.82550048828125, 485.97369384765625, 344.59185791015625]}, {"text": "Chamomilla", "bbox": [91.26399993896484, 362.3185119628906, 147.95358276367188, 375.8857421875]}, {"text": "7 (C14H16)", "bbox": [198.79800415039062, 434.6235046386719, 248.23883056640625, 450.3898620605469]}, {"text": "8 (C15H24)", "bbox": [321.02099609375, 434.6235046386719, 370.4618835449219, 450.3898620605469]}, {"text": "3 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 434.6235046386719, 485.97369384765625, 450.3898620605469]}, {"text": "Artemisia", "bbox": [95.48600006103516, 467.04449462890625, 141.13702392578125, 480.6117248535156]}, {"text": "9 (C10H16O)", "bbox": [194.90899658203125, 536.1334838867188, 252.13063049316406, 551.89990234375]}, {"text": "10 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [314.28399658203125, 536.1334838867188, 377.20166015625, 551.89990234375]}, {"text": "3 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 536.1334838867188, 485.97369384765625, 551.89990234375]}, {"text": "Using chromatography, she determined that the elixir consists of four different substances (X, Y, Z and", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 569.9645385742188, 538.5802612304688, 583.53173828125]}, {"text": "W).", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 581.9194946289062, 71.98444366455078, 595.4866943359375]}, {"text": "The chemist then discovered that X can isomerise into Y in an acidic medium and that Y has a plane of", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 599.8524780273438, 538.5731201171875, 613.419677734375]}, {"text": "symmetry.", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 611.8074951171875, 106.06832885742188, 625.3746948242188]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "1.1", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Identify X and Y.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 195.36964416503906, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 180.1304931640625, 169.74588012695312, 193.69772338867188]}, {"text": "X: 2 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 192.0854949951172, 144.76583862304688, 205.65272521972656]}, {"text": "□1", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 220.92649841308594, 142.6114044189453, 236.18768310546875]}, {"text": "□2", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 220.92649841308594, 209.84640502929688, 236.18768310546875]}, {"text": "□3", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 220.92649841308594, 288.0583801269531, 236.18768310546875]}, {"text": "□4", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 220.92649841308594, 355.29437255859375, 236.18768310546875]}, {"text": "□5", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 220.92649841308594, 429.848388671875, 236.18768310546875]}, {"text": "✓6", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 221.9509735107422, 142.38438415527344, 256.5411071777344]}, {"text": "□7", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 236.8665008544922, 209.84640502929688, 252.127685546875]}, {"text": "□8", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 236.8665008544922, 288.0583801269531, 252.127685546875]}, {"text": "□9", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 236.8665008544922, 355.29437255859375, 252.127685546875]}, {"text": "□10", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 236.8665008544922, 435.5469970703125, 252.127685546875]}, {"text": "Y: 1pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 264.20849609375, 141.5788116455078, 277.7767333984375]}, {"text": "□1", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 293.04949951171875, 142.6114044189453, 308.3106689453125]}, {"text": "□2", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 293.04949951171875, 209.84640502929688, 308.3106689453125]}, {"text": "✓3", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 278.13397216796875, 287.8313903808594, 312.72412109375]}, {"text": "□4", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 293.04949951171875, 355.29437255859375, 308.3106689453125]}, {"text": "□5", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 293.04949951171875, 429.848388671875, 308.3106689453125]}, {"text": "□6", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 308.989501953125, 142.6114044189453, 324.25067138671875]}, {"text": "□7", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 308.989501953125, 209.84640502929688, 324.25067138671875]}, {"text": "□8", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 308.989501953125, 288.0583801269531, 324.25067138671875]}, {"text": "□9", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 308.989501953125, 355.29437255859375, 324.25067138671875]}, {"text": "□10", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 308.989501953125, 435.5469970703125, 324.25067138671875]}, {"text": "1 pt will be given if student switched X and Y.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 336.843505859375, 325.7016296386719, 350.4107360839844]}, {"text": "Linalool (6) isomerises to cineole (3) in acidic solution as follows:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 360.7535095214844, 414.5003356933594, 374.32073974609375]}, {"text": "3.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Chromatography also revealed it was substance Z that gave the elixir its blue colour. Z is a derivative", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5823974609375, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "of the well-known substance A, which has two perpendicular planes of symmetry. When heated, A iso-", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 538.5845336914062, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "merises into aromatic compound B, which has three mutually perpendicular planes of symmetry. When", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 179.12950134277344, 538.5634155273438, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "substance Z is chlorinated, a pair of peaks with an intensity ratio of 3:1 is observed in the mass spectrum", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 191.0854949951172, 538.5729370117188, 204.65272521972656]}, {"text": "at m/z 218 and 220, respectively.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 203.04049682617188, 209.1712188720703, 216.60772705078125]}, {"text": "1.2", "bbox": [78.60796356201172, 226.0054931640625, 92.84230041503906, 239.57272338867188]}, {"text": "Identify Z and draw the structures of substances A and B.", "bbox": [114.6925048828125, 226.0054931640625, 387.8756103515625, 239.57273864746094]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 239.906494140625, 169.74588012695312, 253.47372436523438]}, {"text": "Chlorination of compound Z yields a monochlorinated product whose mass", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 251.86151123046875, 480.57232666015625, 265.4287414550781]}, {"text": "spectrum shows peaks at m/z 218 and 220 in a 3:1 ratio, characteristic of a", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 263.8164978027344, 480.5903625488281, 277.38372802734375]}, {"text": "molecule containing one chlorine atom (reflecting the natural abundance of", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 275.771484375, 480.5699462890625, 289.3387145996094]}, {"text": "35Cl and 37Cl). Therefore, the molecular ion (M) of the 35Cl monochlorinated", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 264.49713134765625, 480.5838623046875, 330.4495544433594]}, {"text": "product is 218, indicating that the non-chlorinated precursor Z has a molec-", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 301.271484375, 480.5804138183594, 314.8387145996094]}, {"text": "ular mass of 184 (218 – 35 + 1 = 184). Compound A is azulene, a hydrocar-", "bbox": [114.6910400390625, 313.22650146484375, 480.58465576171875, 326.7937316894531]}, {"text": "bon distinguished by its deep blue colour – an uncommon property among or-", "bbox": [114.6910400390625, 325.1814880371094, 480.5554504394531, 338.74871826171875]}, {"text": "ganic molecules. Compound Z (𝑀= 184 𝑔mol−1) is identified as chamazulene.", "bbox": [114.6910400390625, 322.2732238769531, 480.5786437988281, 358.51312255859375]}, {"text": "Upon heating, azulene (A) isomerises into naphthalene (B), a thermodynami-", "bbox": [114.69105529785156, 350.7934875488281, 480.5823974609375, 364.3607177734375]}, {"text": "cally more stable isomer.", "bbox": [114.6910400390625, 362.7494812011719, 231.38363647460938, 376.31671142578125]}, {"text": "Z: 1 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 530.1005249023438, 143.72207641601562, 543.667724609375]}, {"text": "□1", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 558.9404907226562, 142.6114044189453, 574.20166015625]}, {"text": "□2", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 558.9404907226562, 209.84640502929688, 574.20166015625]}, {"text": "□3", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 558.9404907226562, 288.0583801269531, 574.20166015625]}, {"text": "□4", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 558.9404907226562, 355.29437255859375, 574.20166015625]}, {"text": "□5", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 558.9404907226562, 429.848388671875, 574.20166015625]}, {"text": "□6", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 574.8815307617188, 142.6114044189453, 590.1427001953125]}, {"text": "✓7", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 559.9660034179688, 209.61940002441406, 594.55615234375]}, {"text": "□8", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 574.8815307617188, 288.0583801269531, 590.1427001953125]}, {"text": "□9", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 574.8815307617188, 355.29437255859375, 590.1427001953125]}, {"text": "□10", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 574.8815307617188, 435.5469970703125, 590.1427001953125]}, {"text": "1 pt for A", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 602.7344970703125, 158.3216094970703, 616.3016967773438]}, {"text": "2 pt for B", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 614.6895141601562, 158.14161682128906, 628.2567138671875]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 225.92950439453125, 521.8194580078125, 239.49673461914062]}, {"text": "The chemist extracted W from the elixir. When W was added to an aqueous Fe3+ solution, a charac-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 628.0362548828125, 538.5848999023438, 659.1675415039062]}, {"text": "teristic colour change was observed. Mass spectrometric analysis of W revealed the intensity ratio of", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 656.3355102539062, 538.5868530273438, 669.9027099609375]}, {"text": "[M]+ ∶[M + 1]+= 9:1, where M is the molecular ion. Assume carbon consists exclusively of 12C and 13C,", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 644.9541625976562, 538.583984375, 710.9065551757812]}, {"text": "the natural isotopic abundance of 12C is 98.9%, and all other elements are monoisotopic.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 666.8642578125, 470.72039794921875, 701.9805297851562]}]}, {"page": 5, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-5", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "1.3", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Determine the number of carbon atoms (𝑛) from the mass spec data and", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 151.31396484375, 480.5740966796875, 185.90411376953125]}, {"text": "identify W. Show your calculations.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 178.18450927734375, 281.8526306152344, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 192.0854949951172, 169.74588012695312, 205.65272521972656]}, {"text": "Since W gives a colour upon reaction with Fe3+, it contains a phenol group. Two", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 179.22213745117188, 480.582763671875, 245.17454528808594]}, {"text": "possible candidates with phenol group are eugenol (C10H12O2) and zingerone", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 191.17813110351562, 480.5835876464844, 257.13055419921875]}, {"text": "(C11H14O3). From mass spec data:", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 203.1331329345703, 274.7189636230469, 269.0855407714844]}, {"text": "0.989𝑛", "bbox": [275.281982421875, 232.49722290039062, 302.154296875, 268.5171203613281]}, {"text": "0.989𝑛−1 × 0.011𝑛", "bbox": [248.29600524902344, 245.57696533203125, 329.6382751464844, 283.53912353515625]}, {"text": "= 9", "bbox": [333.60198974609375, 239.70599365234375, 348.16729736328125, 274.296142578125]}, {"text": "(1)", "bbox": [468.91400146484375, 254.62152099609375, 480.5882263183594, 268.1887512207031]}, {"text": "(n is the number of C atoms in W)", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 278.71051025390625, 270.7558288574219, 292.2777404785156]}, {"text": "𝑛=", "bbox": [254.93699645996094, 289.2599792480469, 269.4724426269531, 323.8501281738281]}, {"text": "0.989", "bbox": [283.92401123046875, 283.48095703125, 306.3398132324219, 318.07110595703125]}, {"text": "0.011 × 9 = 10", "bbox": [273.4429931640625, 289.25994873046875, 340.3305969238281, 330.82513427734375]}, {"text": "meaning that compound W has 10 carbon atoms. Thus, W is eugenol.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 325.9425048828125, 440.75567626953125, 339.5097351074219]}, {"text": "□1", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 354.7825012207031, 142.6114044189453, 370.0436706542969]}, {"text": "□2", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 354.7825012207031, 209.84640502929688, 370.0436706542969]}, {"text": "□3", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 354.7825012207031, 288.0583801269531, 370.0436706542969]}, {"text": "□4", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 354.7825012207031, 355.29437255859375, 370.0436706542969]}, {"text": "✓5", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 339.8669738769531, 429.62139892578125, 374.4571228027344]}, {"text": "□6", "bbox": [126.5780029296875, 370.7235107421875, 142.6114044189453, 385.98468017578125]}, {"text": "□7", "bbox": [193.81399536132812, 370.7235107421875, 209.84640502929688, 385.98468017578125]}, {"text": "□8", "bbox": [272.0249938964844, 370.7235107421875, 288.0583801269531, 385.98468017578125]}, {"text": "□9", "bbox": [339.260986328125, 370.7235107421875, 355.29437255859375, 385.98468017578125]}, {"text": "□10", "bbox": [413.8160095214844, 370.7235107421875, 435.5469970703125, 385.98468017578125]}, {"text": "1 pt for Equation 1", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 398.5765075683594, 201.49293518066406, 412.14373779296875]}, {"text": "(other logically true equations to find carbons atoms will be also considered as", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 410.531494140625, 480.5775451660156, 424.0987243652344]}, {"text": "true)", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 422.4864807128906, 137.16468811035156, 436.0537109375]}, {"text": "1 pt for carbon atoms (n)", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 434.4424743652344, 230.46783447265625, 448.00970458984375]}, {"text": "W: 1 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 446.3974609375, 147.75283813476562, 459.9646911621094]}, {"text": "If student struggled to find number of carbon atoms and choose one of the two", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 458.3524475097656, 480.5473327636719, 471.919677734375]}, {"text": "options (zingerone or eugenol), 1 pt will be given", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 470.30743408203125, 342.95574951171875, 483.8746643066406]}, {"text": "3.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}, {"text": "Part 2. The mysterious stone", "bbox": [56.29199981689453, 507.4375915527344, 213.35301208496094, 522.3616333007812]}, {"text": "Avicenna had told her the stone was a stoichiometric compound. She dissolved it in dilute nitric acid.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 526.4354858398438, 538.5855712890625, 540.002685546875]}, {"text": "After that, she adjusted the pH of the solution to ~4 and added NaF. This led to the formation of pre-", "bbox": [56.69300842285156, 538.3905029296875, 538.5619506835938, 551.9577026367188]}, {"text": "cipitate C ⋅𝑥H2O, which contained 39.16% water by mass. Anhydrous C reacts with an excess of NaF to", "bbox": [56.69300842285156, 535.4299926757812, 538.5809936523438, 570.0201416015625]}, {"text": "yield compound D, which contains 32.85% sodium and 12.85% of metal Q by mass, and is used in the", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 562.3004760742188, 538.57373046875, 575.86767578125]}, {"text": "industrial production of Q.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 574.2554931640625, 180.75863647460938, 587.8226928710938]}]}, {"page": 6, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-6", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "1.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Identify metal Q and compounds C ⋅𝑥H2O and D.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 151.31396484375, 348.12060546875, 185.90411376953125]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 180.1304931640625, 169.74588012695312, 193.69772338867188]}, {"text": "When NaF is added to the solution, precipitate C forms, which dissolves in an ex-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 192.0854949951172, 480.58453369140625, 205.65272521972656]}, {"text": "cess of NaF. This behaviour suggests the formation of a fluoride complex. Since", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 204.04049682617188, 480.56719970703125, 217.60772705078125]}, {"text": "D is used in the production of a metal, and only a few metals are obtained from", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 215.99649047851562, 480.56939697265625, 229.563720703125]}, {"text": "fluoride complexes, the most probable candidates is aluminum. Considering,", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 227.9514923095703, 480.5682067871094, 241.5187225341797]}, {"text": "the ratio of Na:Q in D is 𝑎∶1", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 224.990966796875, 247.23768615722656, 259.58111572265625]}, {"text": "𝑀(Q) =", "bbox": [231.3800048828125, 250.45599365234375, 270.7953796386719, 287.0481262207031]}, {"text": "23𝑎", "bbox": [280.97601318359375, 244.67697143554688, 295.9398193359375, 279.2671203613281]}, {"text": "0.3285 × 0.1285 = 9𝑎", "bbox": [274.7590026855469, 250.45596313476562, 363.88702392578125, 292.0211181640625]}, {"text": "(2)", "bbox": [468.91400146484375, 265.3714904785156, 480.5882263183594, 278.938720703125]}, {"text": "Option a = 3, where Q is aluminum, perfectly fits the conditions.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 287.0824890136719, 412.2105407714844, 300.64971923828125]}, {"text": "C ⋅𝑥H2O is most probably hydrate of aluminum fluoride.", "bbox": [114.6910171508789, 284.1219482421875, 423.9879455566406, 318.71209716796875]}, {"text": "To find", "bbox": [443.2151184082031, 299.0374755859375, 480.5672912597656, 312.6047058105469]}, {"text": "number", "bbox": [114.6910171508789, 310.99249267578125, 152.18115234375, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "of", "bbox": [160.4293212890625, 310.99249267578125, 169.88619995117188, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "water", "bbox": [178.13284301757812, 310.99249267578125, 204.88330078125, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "molecules(𝑥),", "bbox": [213.14141845703125, 296.07696533203125, 275.3696594238281, 330.6671142578125]}, {"text": "we", "bbox": [285.03271484375, 310.99249267578125, 298.4819030761719, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "can", "bbox": [306.7412414550781, 310.99249267578125, 323.27081298828125, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "use", "bbox": [331.5182189941406, 310.99249267578125, 348.0657653808594, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "mass", "bbox": [356.31512451171875, 310.99249267578125, 380.7633972167969, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "fraction", "bbox": [389.0223693847656, 310.99249267578125, 425.19818115234375, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "of", "bbox": [433.4455871582031, 310.99249267578125, 442.9024658203125, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "water,", "bbox": [451.14910888671875, 310.99249267578125, 480.5693054199219, 324.5597229003906]}, {"text": "0.3916 =", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 309.96795654296875, 151.6721954345703, 344.55810546875]}, {"text": "(1.008×2+16)×𝑥", "bbox": [181.46702575683594, 307.5262145996094, 243.61314392089844, 338.6575622558594]}, {"text": "(1.008×2+16)×𝑥+26.98+19×3, 𝑥= 3", "bbox": [155.6439971923828, 309.9679870605469, 298.7043762207031, 348.4385681152344]}, {"text": "Thus, C ⋅𝑥H2O", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 324.9029846191406, 185.06272888183594, 359.4931335449219]}, {"text": "is AlF3.3𝐻2𝑂.", "bbox": [182.48475646972656, 324.9029846191406, 246.03463745117188, 361.0815734863281]}, {"text": "𝑀(D) =", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 339.64398193359375, 150.8623809814453, 374.2391357421875]}, {"text": "27", "bbox": [162.67098999023438, 337.4232177734375, 171.63739013671875, 368.5545654296875]}, {"text": "0.1285 = 210 𝑔mol−1", "bbox": [154.82598876953125, 338.2202453613281, 246.71080017089844, 379.0221252441406]}, {"text": "Thus, D is Na3AlF6.", "bbox": [114.6910171508789, 368.03851318359375, 203.65765380859375, 383.80487060546875]}, {"text": "Q – Al", "bbox": [121.02899932861328, 396.6654968261719, 148.04959106445312, 410.23272705078125]}, {"text": "C ⋅𝑥H2O – AlF3 ⋅3𝐻2𝑂", "bbox": [242.75299072265625, 381.7499694824219, 345.765625, 418.83111572265625]}, {"text": "D – Na3AlF6", "bbox": [364.4779968261719, 396.6654968261719, 420.0267639160156, 412.4318542480469]}, {"text": "1 pt for Equation 2. 1 pt for each correct of Q, C, and D.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 424.1205139160156, 372.5636291503906, 437.687744140625]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}, {"text": "Avicenna told her that he found the stone in a coal deposit. The stone contains the anion of a highly", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 453.8114929199219, 538.5711059570312, 467.37872314453125]}, {"text": "symmetrical acid F. Reaction of F with P2O5 gives binary compound G, which contains 49.98% of oxygen", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 465.7664794921875, 538.5921630859375, 481.82470703125]}, {"text": "by mass and has a three-fold symmetry axis. F can be prepared by oxidising compound E with potassium", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 477.7214660644531, 538.5803833007812, 491.2886962890625]}, {"text": "permanganate in an acidic solution. E contains 11.18% of hydrogen by mass and has a six-fold symmetry", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 489.67645263671875, 538.5767822265625, 503.2436828613281]}, {"text": "axis.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 501.6324462890625, 77.56526947021484, 515.1996459960938]}]}, {"page": 7, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-7", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "1.5", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of E, F, and G.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 276.1466064453125, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 178.18450927734375, 169.74588012695312, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "The highly symmetrical nature of the unknown compounds suggests that these", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 190.1405029296875, 480.55731201171875, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "are carboxylic derivatives of benzene, which form anhydrides when treated with", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 202.0955047607422, 480.56915283203125, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "phosphorus pentoxide. Thus, for G:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 214.05050659179688, 280.7986145019531, 227.61773681640625]}, {"text": "C∶O = 50.02", "bbox": [233.89801025390625, 214.817138671875, 287.58282470703125, 280.7695617675781]}, {"text": "12.01 ∶49.98", "bbox": [265.1669921875, 218.9409637451172, 323.0158386230469, 266.28411865234375]}, {"text": "16", "bbox": [306.82598876953125, 231.6939697265625, 316.7886047363281, 266.28411865234375]}, {"text": "= 1.333", "bbox": [326.97900390625, 218.9409637451172, 360.18182373046875, 259.31011962890625]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [346.4840087890625, 231.6939697265625, 351.4653015136719, 266.28411865234375]}, {"text": "The corresponding minimum integer ratio is 4:3 (C4O3). Considering that F is", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 236.47412109375, 480.5864562988281, 302.4265441894531]}, {"text": "a carboxylic acid and G is its anhydride, the presence of symmetry, and the", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 273.24749755859375, 480.5719299316406, 286.8147277832031]}, {"text": "aromatic nature of these compounds, one can propose that: G is C12O9, mellitic", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 260.3841552734375, 480.58380126953125, 326.3365783691406]}, {"text": "acid anhydride. F is C6(COOH)6, mellitic acid. Treatment of E with potassium", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 272.3391418457031, 480.583740234375, 338.29156494140625]}, {"text": "permanganate leads to F (mellitic acid), indicating that E is a hexasubstituted", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 309.11248779296875, 480.59344482421875, 322.6797180175781]}, {"text": "benzene.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 321.0685119628906, 157.34153747558594, 334.6357421875]}, {"text": "0.1118 =", "bbox": [243.31100463867188, 331.61798095703125, 280.2921447753906, 366.2081298828125]}, {"text": "1.008𝑥", "bbox": [303.5690002441406, 325.8389892578125, 331.4642333984375, 360.42913818359375]}, {"text": "1.008𝑥+ 12.01𝑦", "bbox": [284.2640075683594, 338.59197998046875, 350.7643127441406, 373.18212890625]}, {"text": "(3)", "bbox": [468.91400146484375, 346.53350830078125, 480.5882263183594, 360.1007385253906]}, {"text": "Solving this equation gives, x:y=9:6 Thus, the empirical formula of E is C6H9.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 345.1091613769531, 480.58465576171875, 411.06158447265625]}, {"text": "The number of H atoms must be even, so, C12H18 or (C6(CH3)6) ideally fits the", "bbox": [114.6910400390625, 357.06414794921875, 480.5843200683594, 423.0165710449219]}, {"text": "conditions. Thus, E is (C6(CH3)6).", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 369.0191345214844, 267.6673583984375, 434.9715576171875]}, {"text": "0.5 pt for finding C:O ratio in G", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 556.8054809570312, 257.7921447753906, 570.3726806640625]}, {"text": "2 pt for structure of G", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 568.760498046875, 216.5361328125, 582.3276977539062]}, {"text": "2 pt for structure of F", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 580.7155151367188, 214.78976440429688, 594.28271484375]}, {"text": "0.5 pt for Equation 3", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 592.6705322265625, 209.86151123046875, 606.2377319335938]}, {"text": "0.5 pt for empirical formula of E", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 604.6255493164062, 263.503662109375, 618.1927490234375]}, {"text": "1.5 pt for structure of E", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 616.58056640625, 223.26864624023438, 630.1477661132812]}, {"text": "(full marks will be given if student did not show calculations but did find all", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 628.5365600585938, 480.56561279296875, 642.103759765625]}, {"text": "structures correctly)", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 640.4915771484375, 208.44711303710938, 654.0587768554688]}, {"text": "7.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}, {"text": "Then, she analysed the stone thermogravimetrically in open air. A 10.00 g sample began to lose mass", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 664.8289794921875, 538.5748291015625, 699.4191284179688]}, {"text": "at approximately 100 ∘C and stopped at 5.75 g at 200 ∘C. A second drop in mass was observed at 400 ∘C,", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 666.8811645507812, 538.5826416015625, 732.8335571289062]}, {"text": "with a final mass of 1.50 g of compound H remaining constant at higher temperatures.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 703.654541015625, 462.03106689453125, 717.2217407226562]}]}, {"page": 8, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-8", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "1.6", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Determine the chemical formulae of the stone and compound H using ther-", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 480.5766906738281, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "mogravimetric data.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 178.18450927734375, 209.55555725097656, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 190.1405029296875, 169.74588012695312, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "Thermogravimetric data indicate that the mineral is a hydrate, as it starts to", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 202.0955047607422, 480.58734130859375, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "lose mass at about 100 °C. Thus, the molecular formula of the stone would be", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 214.05050659179688, 480.5671691894531, 227.61773681640625]}, {"text": "Al2(C6(COO)6) ⋅𝑛H2O. Thus,", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 201.18714904785156, 245.84271240234375, 267.1395568847656]}, {"text": "4.25", "bbox": [214.23500061035156, 230.89599609375, 231.66952514648438, 265.48614501953125]}, {"text": "(1.008 × 2 + 16)𝑛=", "bbox": [187.45098876953125, 236.67498779296875, 269.24237060546875, 278.2391357421875]}, {"text": "5.75", "bbox": [331.7980041503906, 230.89596557617188, 349.2325439453125, 265.4861145019531]}, {"text": "26.98 × 2 + 12.01 × 12 + 16 × 12", "bbox": [273.20501708984375, 243.64898681640625, 407.819580078125, 278.2391357421875]}, {"text": "(4)", "bbox": [468.91400146484375, 251.59051513671875, 480.5882263183594, 265.1577453613281]}, {"text": "n = 16", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 274.5164794921875, 143.1121063232422, 288.0837097167969]}, {"text": "The final decomposition product is most likely aluminum oxide. To confirm this:", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 286.47149658203125, 480.5781555175781, 300.0387268066406]}, {"text": "1.50", "bbox": [214.23500061035156, 291.3619689941406, 231.66952514648438, 325.9521179199219]}, {"text": "𝑀", "bbox": [217.4980010986328, 304.1149597167969, 227.51040649414062, 338.7051086425781]}, {"text": "=", "bbox": [235.63299560546875, 297.1409606933594, 242.45738220214844, 331.7311096191406]}, {"text": "5.75", "bbox": [305.01300048828125, 291.3619384765625, 322.4475402832031, 325.95208740234375]}, {"text": "26.98 × 2 + 12.01 × 12 + 16 × 12", "bbox": [246.42100524902344, 304.1149597167969, 381.0355529785156, 338.7051086425781]}, {"text": "(5)", "bbox": [468.91400146484375, 312.0564880371094, 480.5882263183594, 325.62371826171875]}, {"text": "M = 101.8 𝑔mol−1, which is very close to the molar mass of Al2O3.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 311.98114013671875, 422.8296203613281, 377.9335632324219]}, {"text": "Thus, H - Al2O3", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 323.9361267089844, 186.0412139892578, 389.8885498046875]}, {"text": "Stone: Al2(C6(COO)6) ⋅16H2O (Honeystone)", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 335.89111328125, 320.0971374511719, 401.8435363769531]}, {"text": "1 pt for Equation 4", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 384.6195068359375, 201.49293518066406, 398.1867370605469]}, {"text": "1 pt for Equation 5", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 408.5304870605469, 201.49293518066406, 422.09771728515625]}, {"text": "1 pt for the formula of the stone", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 432.4404602050781, 267.0785827636719, 446.0076904296875]}, {"text": "1 pt for the formula of the compound H", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 456.3504333496094, 300.1427307128906, 469.91766357421875]}, {"text": "(full marks will be given if student found both formulae correctly without show-", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 468.3064270019531, 480.57525634765625, 481.8736572265625]}, {"text": "ing any equations).", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 480.26141357421875, 203.8170623779297, 493.8286437988281]}, {"text": "If student has incorrect Q and/or incorrect F then credit can be given only if they", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 492.2164001464844, 480.5847473144531, 505.78363037109375]}, {"text": "propose an alternative answer that is consistent with the data and chemically", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 504.17138671875, 480.5574035644531, 517.7385864257812]}, {"text": "sensible.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 516.1264038085938, 158.13941955566406, 529.693603515625]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}]